.TH AILX 1 "2026-11-27" "ailx 0.1" "AI Linux"
.SH NAME
ailx \- AI Linux system layer: inventory, diagnosis, profiles, transactions, engines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ailx
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-nvml\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Commands: \fBstatus\fR, \fBhardware\fR, \fBresources\fR, \fBdoctor\fR, \fBknobs\fR,
\fBprofile\fR list|show|plan|apply, \fBconfirm\fR, \fBrollback\fR [\-\-recover], \fBhistory\fR,
\fBengine\fR list|install|verify|use|remove|env, \fBimage\fR status|stage|confirm|rollback,
\fBsystem\fR plan|install|uninstall|sudoers.
.PP
Profile settings that are not hardware-validated are experimental and are only applied with
\fB\-\-include\-experimental\fR. Every change is journaled, verified and can be rolled back;
privileged writes go through \fI/usr/libexec/ailx/ailx-apply-helper\fR.
.SH FILES
/etc/ailx/ailx.toml, /var/lib/ailx (state, engines, models)
.SH SEE ALSO
ailx-bench(1)
